{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1485893445,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NjQ3NzYzNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-276477634"},"message":"Adding:\n\n````\nimport os\nos.environ['GIT_SSH_COMMAND'] = \"datalad sshrun\"\n````\n\ndoesn't change a things -- as @bpoldrack predicted.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486048106,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3Njk4Mjg1Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-276982856"},"message":"Figured it out with @mih. Fix included in #1237.\n\nIn case we need a reminder when we run into a similar thing:\nKey issue was, that we share connections with annex. Therefore in the case annex (instead of datalad) creates the connection to be used, remote sensing of annex_install_dir wasn't done. So `datalad sshrun` was called, but didn't lead to `SSHConnection` passing the corrected `PATH` to the remote command.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486048676,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3Njk4NTYwMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-276985602"},"message":"Thinking about this more: I assume that any annex command that executes remote git calls would make an attempt to run its own bundled Git -- if any exists. If that is the case, this is nothing to worry about. However, if that is not the case, we should make an effort to open connections ourselves.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486051796,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzAwMTA5MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-277001090"},"message":"I kind of agree.\nHowever, this would probably not be about opening the connection anymore (since this is fixed now), but about executing git-annex calls the same way (via `datalad sshrun`).\n\nI'll try to examine this to be sure.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486094897,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzE2MDAxMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-277160012"},"message":"Looking into it, I think we need to use `datalad sshrun` with annex, too.\nWith `annex sync` for example I used `GIT_SSH_COMMAND=\"cat\"` in order to see what is passed to it and this is plain `git-upload-pack`, `git-receive-pack`. No `PATH`passed or `sendenv` used. I don't see how annex could possibly ensure to use the bundled git on the remote that way.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486095919,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzE2MTczNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-277161736"},"message":"BTW: The above mentioned might be the issue, leading to several failures in PR #1237 , where system-git is used that is too old for `config receive.denyCurrentBranch updateInstead`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486104502,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzE3Njk0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-277176949"},"message":"Damn\n\nhttps://travis-ci.org/datalad/datalad/jobs/197904584\n\nThis actually happens (at least for one test) in a GitRepo.push() call, that should really really not result in a system-git call. It seems it is still not working on travis.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486105070,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzE3ODA4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-277178080"},"message":"Ok, this:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/1237/commits/6794e9d6761bbed123cfe506448fa2f9deb98162\n\nhopefully makes git annex use sshrun for most (if not all) cases.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1486128274,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3NzI0NTcyOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-277245729"},"message":"Brutal approach but might work ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487070898,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY3OTY3OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1247#issuecomment-279679679"},"message":"Okay, for one thing the title doesn't describe the actual issue correctly and furthermore this seems to be solved for now.\nThus - closing.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487070899,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTYxMTg4NzE5"},"status":2}]}